[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:Not Guilty]
[00:00.58]Lesson 11 | 第11课
[00:01.93]Not guilty | 无罪
[00:03.84]What was the Customs Officer looking for? | 海关官员在找什么？
[00:12.52]Customs Officers are quite tolerant these days, but they can still stop you when you are going through the Green Channel and have nothing to declare. | 如今海关官员相当宽容，但当你走绿色通道并且没有东西要申报时，他们仍然可以拦住你。
[00:22.58]Even really honest people are often made to feel guilty. | 即使是非常诚实的人也常常会感到内疚。
[00:27.20]The hardened professional smuggler, on the other hand, is never troubled by such feelings, | 另一方面，那些老练的职业走私犯从不会被这种感觉所困扰，
[00:33.44]even if he has five hundred gold watches hidden in his suitcase. | 即使他的手提箱里藏着五百块金表。
[00:38.48]When I returned from abroad recently, a particularly officious young Customs Officer | 最近我从国外回来时，一位特别爱管闲事的年轻海关官员
[00:44.80]clearly regarded me as a smuggler. | 显然把我当成了走私犯。
[00:47.74]'Have you anything to declare?' he asked, looking me in the eye. | “你有什么要申报的吗？”他直视着我的眼睛问道。
[00:53.78]'No,' I answered confidently. | “没有，”我自信地回答道。
[00:57.30]'Would you mind unlocking this suitcase please? ' | “请您打开这个手提箱好吗？”
[01:00.98]'Not at all,' I answered. | “当然可以，”我回答道。
[01:03.75]The Officer went through the case with great care. | 那个官员非常仔细地检查了箱子。
[01:07.38]All the things I had packed so carefully were soon in a dreadful mess. | 我费尽心思整理好的所有东西很快就乱七八糟了。
[01:13.18]I felt sure I would never be able to close the case again. | 我确信我再也无法把箱子合上了。
[01:17.86]Suddenly, I saw the Officer's face light up. | 突然，我看到那个官员的脸上露出了喜色。
[01:22.02]He had spotted a tiny bottle at the bottom of my case | 他发现了一个小瓶子在我的箱子底部
[01:26.14]and he pounced on it with delight. | 他欣喜若狂地扑了上去。
[01:28.90]'Perfume, eh?' he asked sarcastically. | “香水，嗯？”他挖苦地问道。
[01:33.99]'You should have declared that. | “你应该申报那个。
[01:36.52]Perfume is not exempt from import duty. ' | 香水不免除进口关税。”
[01:40.70]'But it isn't perfume, I said. 'It's hair gel. ' | “但它不是香水，”我说，“它是发胶。”
[01:46.58]Then I added with a smile, | 然后我笑着补充道，
[01:49.22]'It's a strange mixture I make myself. | “这是我自己调制的一种奇怪的混合物。”
[01:52.85]As I expected, he did not believe me. | 如我所料，他没有相信我。
[01:56.80]'Try it!' I said encouragingly. | “尝尝看！”我鼓励地说。
[02:00.52]The Officer unscrewed the cap and put the bottle to his nostrils. | 那个官员拧开瓶盖，把瓶子凑到鼻孔前。
[02:05.26]He was greeted by an unpleasant smell which convinced him that I was telling the truth. | 一股难闻的气味扑鼻而来，这让他相信我说的是实话。
[02:11.53]A few minutes later, I was able to hurry away with precious chalk marks on my baggage. | 几分钟后，我带着行李上珍贵的粉笔标记，匆匆离开了。